# secret-scan allowlist (honored by ~/.config/git/hooks/pre-push via
# scripts/ci/secret_scan.py). One path glob per line; '#' starts a comment.
#
# Generated golden fixtures are deterministic generator output (synthetic test
# data produced by scripts/golden.sh), not hand-authored source. They embed Go
# struct field names and config keys that pattern-match as credentials but hold
# no real values. The specs (catalog/specs/) and generator source stay scanned;
# only the generated expected tree is skipped.
testdata/golden/expected/**

# QuickBooks OAuth codegen surfaces: the underscore form of "client secret"
# in these files is the RFC 6749 FIELD NAME (spec keys, string comparisons,
# placeholder maps, doc examples), never a value — values are runtime-env
# only. Pattern 'client-secret-field' false-positives on the literal, the
# scanner has no line-level suppression, and the field name cannot be
# reworded where it appears in code and spec keys. Prose-only occurrences
# (e.g. generator.go comments) are reworded instead of allowlisted.
# (2026-07-05 workspace-cleanup knockout; narrowed 2026-07-08 per codex P1)
